## 6. API testing

**Standard:** Use Playwright `{ request }` for setup/teardown helpers and contract checks; prefer `trackProgram` for program lifecycle; never hardcode tokens.

✅ **Good** *(advised — no dedicated contract spec in repo yet; see `playwright-api-fixture` skill)*:

```typescript
import { test, expect } from '../fixtures/cleanup.fixture';

test('GET /api/programs returns data array', { tag: '@api-contract' }, async ({ request }) => {
  const res = await request.get('/api/programs', {
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.DIDAXIS_API_TOKEN}` },
  });
  expect(res.ok()).toBeTruthy();
  expect(Array.isArray((await res.json()).data)).toBe(true);
});
```

❌ **Bad:**

```typescript
const token = 'eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIs…';           // hardcoded secret
test.afterAll(async () => { await deleteAllPrograms(); });  // manual teardown
```

**Why:** Hardcoded tokens leak credentials and rot; manual `afterAll` cleanup skips on failure mid-test and fights parallel isolation.

