## 8. Accessibility

**Standard:** Axe scan with `.withTags(['wcag2a','wcag2aa'])` on key pages plus a separate keyboard test (Tab → `toBeFocused()` → Enter opens dialog); POM locators only; one `{ tag: '@a11y-*' }` per test; report real violations — never `.disableRules()` to go green.

✅ **Good** *(advised target — replace `tests/programs.a11y.spec.ts` fixme pattern; see `a11y-checks` skill)*:

```typescript
test('Programs page WCAG 2 A/AA', { tag: '@a11y-axe-programs-page' }, async ({ page }) => {
  await programsPage.goto();
  const results = await new AxeBuilder({ page }).withTags(['wcag2a', 'wcag2aa']).analyze();
  await expect(results.violations).toEqual([]);
});

test('Tab+Enter opens New Program', { tag: '@a11y-keyboard-new-program' }, async ({ page }) => {
  await programsPage.goto();
  // tab until programsPage.newProgramButton focused …
  await expect(programsPage.newProgramButton).toBeFocused();
  await page.keyboard.press('Enter');
  await expect(programsPage.newProgramModal.dialog).toBeVisible();
});
```

❌ **Bad** (from `tests/programs.a11y.spec.ts` — do not copy):

```typescript
const results = await new AxeBuilder({ page })
  .disableRules('color-contrast')   // silences real failures
  .analyze();
expect(results.violations).toEqual([]);  // bare expect, no WCAG tags
```

**Why:** Disabling rules hides WCAG defects; missing keyboard tests leaves focus order unverified; axe alone cannot catch Tab/Enter activation.

